WEBVTT

00:06.297 --> 00:08.299
[theme music playing]

00:29.070 --> 00:30.238
[line ringing]

00:41.875 --> 00:46.963
WHEN THE PHONE RINGS

00:47.046 --> 00:48.965
EPISODE 8

00:49.591 --> 00:50.884
[solemn music playing]

01:19.829 --> 01:20.830
[chuckles softly]

01:23.416 --> 01:25.418
[soft song playing]

01:48.775 --> 01:49.776
[Sa-eon] Thank you…

01:50.693 --> 01:52.487
for all your hard work, 406.

01:52.570 --> 01:53.655
You…

01:55.865 --> 01:57.242
knew everything?

01:58.660 --> 02:00.161
Since when? No…

02:02.205 --> 02:04.415
If you knew, why didn't you…

02:05.500 --> 02:06.459
Why didn't I what?

02:08.086 --> 02:09.671
[voice shaking] Why didn't you hate me?

02:10.380 --> 02:11.297
Tell me…

02:14.968 --> 02:15.885
Hong Hee-joo.

02:18.221 --> 02:20.140
Tell me how to hate you.

02:21.933 --> 02:24.018
Tell me how to not love you.

02:25.520 --> 02:27.021
[soft song continues playing]

02:45.582 --> 02:46.583
[song ends]

02:51.379 --> 02:53.339
[pleasant music playing]

03:10.523 --> 03:11.691
Eat slowly.

03:20.575 --> 03:21.659
It's good.

03:21.743 --> 03:22.702
[chuckles softly]

03:22.785 --> 03:25.830
[Hee-joo] I've been wondering for a while,
but why are you such a good cook?

03:26.623 --> 03:27.707
[inhales deeply]

03:27.790 --> 03:29.417
Cooking's about sincerity.

03:30.668 --> 03:33.421
To tell the truth,
as long as the kimchi's good,

03:33.504 --> 03:35.632
this dish is a success.

03:39.469 --> 03:40.511
It's really good.

03:40.595 --> 03:42.222
[pleasant music continues playing]

03:42.764 --> 03:43.723
From now on,

03:44.933 --> 03:46.267
let's eat together often.

03:46.851 --> 03:47.685
At home.

03:48.478 --> 03:50.355
So it'll feel more like a home

03:52.106 --> 03:53.566
and not feel like a jail.

03:53.650 --> 03:56.694
When did I call it a jail?
That's what you said.

03:57.362 --> 03:59.781
- I did?
- You just feel guilty.

04:00.406 --> 04:02.158
No, I don't.

04:02.242 --> 04:04.744
Was the three years
we lived together normal?

04:04.827 --> 04:07.330
There were nothing but cold vibes
in this house.

04:08.039 --> 04:10.625
We didn't speak or make eye contact.

04:10.708 --> 04:12.794
We didn't eat or sleep together…

04:21.719 --> 04:22.553
Do you want that?

04:24.973 --> 04:25.848
[chuckles softly]

04:27.934 --> 04:30.186
If you hated sleeping in separate rooms,

04:31.354 --> 04:32.647
you should've told me.

04:32.730 --> 04:35.650
No, that's not what I'm saying.

04:38.236 --> 04:40.071
To me… [sighs]

04:41.281 --> 04:42.615
this home was warm.

04:42.699 --> 04:44.450
[slow music playing]

04:49.247 --> 04:50.581
When I returned home

04:51.916 --> 04:53.835
and saw the lights in the window,

04:55.420 --> 04:56.587
it made me feel good

04:57.547 --> 04:58.715
to know you were there.

05:13.271 --> 05:14.856
When I looked at you,

05:15.773 --> 05:17.692
the noisy world around me

05:18.985 --> 05:20.445
became quiet…

05:21.696 --> 05:23.031
and peaceful.

05:24.741 --> 05:26.617
You should've told me sooner.

05:27.201 --> 05:28.369
Do you remember

05:29.245 --> 05:30.913
what I said to you before?

05:32.040 --> 05:33.458
I told you

05:34.417 --> 05:36.336
not to have any feelings for me.

05:37.045 --> 05:40.131
Don't try to have any feelings for me.

05:41.299 --> 05:42.467
Let it all go.

05:42.550 --> 05:45.386
You don't need to act like a puppet
in front of me.

05:46.304 --> 05:47.847
How could I forget that?

05:47.930 --> 05:50.475
You didn't have to be so harsh.

05:51.642 --> 05:52.602
[inhales deeply]

05:53.478 --> 05:54.729
I was scared.

05:55.730 --> 05:57.732
If I didn't draw the line like that,

05:59.275 --> 06:01.611
I was scared
I'd end up giving you my heart,

06:02.278 --> 06:05.490
and before I knew it,
I'd think living like this with you

06:06.949 --> 06:08.284
might actually be okay.

06:10.328 --> 06:12.580
That I'd give up everything
and just cave in.

06:15.291 --> 06:16.793
[Sa-eon] Let me be clear.

06:16.876 --> 06:18.252
You weren't part of my plan.

06:18.336 --> 06:19.378
So from now on,

06:20.463 --> 06:22.673
if you interfere or get in my way,

06:23.758 --> 06:24.717
I won't let it slide.

06:26.302 --> 06:27.637
What was the plan

06:28.596 --> 06:30.306
you mentioned back then?

06:30.389 --> 06:31.933
[slow music continues playing]

06:32.850 --> 06:34.435
[clicks tongue, inhales deeply]

06:34.936 --> 06:37.605
I'll tell you when the time comes.

06:42.485 --> 06:43.486
Actually…

06:45.822 --> 06:47.532
I have something to tell you too.

06:52.787 --> 06:54.914
UNKNOWN CALLER

06:57.333 --> 06:58.459
[inhales deeply]

06:59.836 --> 07:00.670
Relax.

07:01.587 --> 07:02.713
Don't worry anymore.

07:03.339 --> 07:05.675
I will track him down soon.

07:06.634 --> 07:09.387
Also, about this phone,

07:10.638 --> 07:12.598
only you and I know about it.

07:12.682 --> 07:14.392
It's not going to the police.

07:15.184 --> 07:16.310
That'll never happen.

07:16.394 --> 07:18.938
Are you worried it'll be revealed
that I'm involved?

07:20.523 --> 07:21.649
I'm prepared for it.

07:22.984 --> 07:24.694
Let's reveal everything and--

07:24.777 --> 07:27.029
I'm going to take care of things
one by one.

07:27.530 --> 07:28.698
You just wait.

07:29.407 --> 07:31.325
Don't think about doing anything.

07:31.409 --> 07:32.994
And for the time being,

07:33.911 --> 07:37.206
don't speak in front of anyone but me.

07:39.041 --> 07:39.876
Why not?

07:39.959 --> 07:43.004
The accomplice is someone close to us.
I'm sure of it.

07:43.087 --> 07:45.089
Until we know exactly who it is,

07:45.798 --> 07:46.799
we must be careful.

07:49.260 --> 07:50.344
Okay.

07:53.055 --> 07:54.599
[inhales deeply]

07:55.475 --> 07:57.143
[Sa-eon] To tell you the truth,

07:58.394 --> 07:59.812
I'm sad to end these calls.

08:00.480 --> 08:01.522
It was fun.

08:02.523 --> 08:04.859
The fiery Hong Hee-joo that only shows up

08:05.860 --> 08:07.361
when she's 406.

08:08.654 --> 08:10.990
Wait, where was that lingerie again?

08:13.451 --> 08:14.911
[Hee-joo] Why? No, wait.

08:19.081 --> 08:20.708
[slow music playing]

08:30.051 --> 08:30.885
Why?

08:32.220 --> 08:33.095
It's just…

08:34.055 --> 08:35.598
hard to believe.

08:37.058 --> 08:40.561
That you accepted me just as I am

08:41.145 --> 08:42.730
and forgave me.

08:49.570 --> 08:51.572
[gripping music playing]

09:01.832 --> 09:03.417
[Sa-eon] Could you do the same

09:05.294 --> 09:07.004
when you know everything about me?

09:07.964 --> 09:09.382
[rain pattering]

09:19.767 --> 09:20.768
[phone vibrates]

09:21.644 --> 09:22.645
[sighs softly]

09:28.442 --> 09:30.236
MASTER
DID YOU GET THE PHONE BACK?

09:33.322 --> 09:34.323
[kidnapper] No.

09:35.157 --> 09:36.617
WHY NOT?

09:36.701 --> 09:38.703
[mysterious music playing]

09:43.499 --> 09:44.834
[tires screech]

10:08.774 --> 10:10.359
[kidnapper] What the hell?

10:12.737 --> 10:14.238
Damn it.

10:16.616 --> 10:17.617
[sighs]

10:29.879 --> 10:31.505
[man] Just a moment!

10:32.715 --> 10:33.674
Goodness.

10:33.758 --> 10:34.675
Good grief.

10:34.759 --> 10:36.510
Oh, goodness.

10:39.972 --> 10:41.849
Oh, boy. My goodness.

10:42.767 --> 10:44.560
- Goodness.
- What floor?

10:44.644 --> 10:46.228
Thank you. I'm going to B4.

10:46.312 --> 10:47.229
I see.

10:50.399 --> 10:51.567
[man] Thank you.

10:53.277 --> 10:54.278
Goodness.

10:55.029 --> 10:57.573
Aren't you Spokesperson Paik Sa-eon?

10:57.657 --> 10:58.866
[chuckles softly] Yes.

10:58.949 --> 11:01.369
It's an honor to meet you.

11:01.452 --> 11:03.704
I saw the news. Are you okay?

11:03.788 --> 11:07.416
The world's so chaotic
that all sorts of weird people

11:07.500 --> 11:09.502
dare to do things like that to you.

11:10.503 --> 11:13.547
- Thank you for your concern.
- [man] Take care of yourself.

11:14.382 --> 11:16.884
Such a bad guy
should be caught… [voice fades]

11:16.967 --> 11:18.511
[suspenseful music playing]

11:26.936 --> 11:28.229
[kidnapper sniffs]

11:29.146 --> 11:30.314
[kidnapper] Did you know?

11:31.565 --> 11:33.067
Paik Sa-eon

11:34.735 --> 11:37.113
smells really good.

11:43.619 --> 11:44.620
[sighs wearily]

11:49.708 --> 11:50.626
[groans]

11:50.709 --> 11:54.839
What I want to get back
isn't that stupid phone.

11:57.675 --> 11:58.509
[scoffs]

11:58.592 --> 12:00.136
[gripping music playing]

12:03.597 --> 12:04.890
I'm going to take it all.

12:05.683 --> 12:08.269
Even the scent coming from him.

12:18.070 --> 12:21.657
The screen beside me shows
the composite sketch of the suspect.

12:22.241 --> 12:23.701
According to police,

12:23.784 --> 12:26.871
the suspect is around 185 cm tall
with a solid build

12:26.954 --> 12:29.165
and in his early to mid-thirties.

12:29.248 --> 12:34.003
And he is odd-eyed, and one eye
appears light brown in different lighting.

12:34.086 --> 12:37.673
He has also been reported
to have anger management issues,

12:37.756 --> 12:41.469
acting impulsively
due to a lack of control.

12:41.552 --> 12:42.678
Sir. Ma'am.

12:43.387 --> 12:44.847
HBC has reached out to confirm

12:44.930 --> 12:47.475
if the interview will proceed
as scheduled.

12:47.558 --> 12:49.226
[suspenseful music playing]

12:49.894 --> 12:51.061
- Cancel it.
- Say we'll do it.

12:56.275 --> 12:57.234
Yes, ma'am.

13:03.824 --> 13:04.867
Mr. Min.

13:04.950 --> 13:06.076
Yes, sir?

13:10.748 --> 13:12.666
[inaudible]

13:12.750 --> 13:13.751
[music ends]

13:19.590 --> 13:20.799
[groans softly]

13:52.706 --> 13:54.375
[somber music playing]

13:58.712 --> 14:00.839
[automated voice]
The number you dialed doesn't exist.

14:00.923 --> 14:04.218
- Please check the number and try again.
- [exhales deeply]

14:07.096 --> 14:10.391
[automated voice]
The number you dialed doesn't exist.

14:10.474 --> 14:12.476
- Please check…
- [line disconnects]

14:13.686 --> 14:16.772
[automated voice]
The number you dialed doesn't exist.

14:16.855 --> 14:17.690
Please check…

14:18.274 --> 14:19.108
[music ends]

14:19.191 --> 14:20.568
[breathing heavily]

14:24.864 --> 14:26.156
[mellow music playing]

14:32.413 --> 14:33.706
[breathing heavily]

15:10.743 --> 15:12.494
[mellow music continues playing]

15:23.464 --> 15:24.465
[music ends]

15:29.553 --> 15:31.013
Did you sleep well?

15:36.185 --> 15:38.854
Aren't you going to work?

15:39.563 --> 15:40.981
Not today.

15:44.360 --> 15:46.195
I won't move an inch today.

15:47.154 --> 15:48.322
I took the day off.

15:50.866 --> 15:52.284
You did?

15:52.368 --> 15:53.535
[inhales deeply]

15:55.788 --> 15:57.039
As you know,

15:58.207 --> 15:59.708
for the past three years,

15:59.792 --> 16:01.752
I've worked without any days off,

16:01.835 --> 16:03.796
even on holidays and weekends.

16:04.922 --> 16:06.548
I can take a day off.

16:08.467 --> 16:09.301
Then…

16:10.052 --> 16:11.804
what will you do today?

16:16.016 --> 16:17.476
Is there something you want to do?

16:19.853 --> 16:21.105
[Hee-joo] Well…

16:22.606 --> 16:24.149
[pleasant music playing]

16:24.233 --> 16:25.401
There is.

16:25.484 --> 16:29.405
Things that I never imagined
we could do together.

16:34.034 --> 16:35.411
I know it's ridiculous,

16:36.495 --> 16:38.872
but I imagined it sometimes.

16:42.209 --> 16:43.794
[speaking indistinctly]

16:44.378 --> 16:45.754
[both laughing]

16:47.715 --> 16:49.049
[Hee-joo] Us being…

16:50.175 --> 16:52.428
completely ordinary
just like everyone else.

17:11.739 --> 17:12.906
Funny, right?

17:12.990 --> 17:17.619
Even though I wanted to get a divorce
and to escape this house every day.

17:17.703 --> 17:19.121
[soft song playing]

17:26.295 --> 17:27.421
Since when?

17:29.006 --> 17:29.840
What?

17:29.923 --> 17:33.052
When did you start imagining that?

17:33.135 --> 17:34.428
I don't know.

17:38.348 --> 17:39.391
Probably…

17:48.192 --> 17:49.026
[Sa-eon] She is…

17:50.861 --> 17:52.029
my wife.

17:52.988 --> 17:55.365
Did you fall for me then?

17:55.449 --> 17:57.367
[chuckling] Fall for you? Me?

17:58.285 --> 18:02.206
It's just that I'd never thought
you'd do something like that.

18:03.207 --> 18:04.333
For me,

18:05.667 --> 18:07.544
it was way before that.

18:09.338 --> 18:11.090
Way before.

18:12.633 --> 18:13.550
When?

18:15.886 --> 18:17.054
[Sa-eon] Well…

18:27.898 --> 18:28.774
[phone vibrating]

18:34.196 --> 18:35.197
[sighs wearily]

18:42.329 --> 18:44.039
CHIEF KANG YOUNG-WOO

18:44.123 --> 18:45.457
- [phone vibrating]
- [Sa-eon sighs]

18:46.959 --> 18:47.960
[clears throat]

18:50.003 --> 18:51.421
- Yes?
- [Young-woo] Mr. Paik?

18:52.131 --> 18:54.925
- Sorry for disturbing you on your day off.
- What is it?

18:55.008 --> 18:58.428
I'm really sorry, but I think
you need to come here right away.

18:59.263 --> 19:00.681
[solemn music playing]

19:02.432 --> 19:03.684
[sighs]

19:04.351 --> 19:06.812
- [reporter 1] A car's coming!
- [reporter 2] He's here!

19:09.106 --> 19:11.692
- [reporter 3] Wait.
- [bodyguard 1] Move out of the way.

19:11.775 --> 19:13.360
[bodyguard 2] Move. Just a moment.

19:13.443 --> 19:14.820
- Please move.
- [bodyguard 3] Move.

19:14.903 --> 19:16.446
Move out of the way.

19:16.530 --> 19:18.532
[reporter 4] Why was Paik Sa-eon
being threatened?

19:18.615 --> 19:21.201
[reporter 5] Who do you think
is the mastermind behind them?

19:21.285 --> 19:25.038
Paik Sa-eon's statement
was completely different from your claims.

19:25.122 --> 19:26.540
Could you comment on that?

19:26.623 --> 19:27.875
[gripping music playing]

19:28.750 --> 19:29.751
Why do you think that is?

19:31.044 --> 19:32.671
The spokesperson

19:33.297 --> 19:37.092
drew a clear line to avoid causing
any trouble to his father's future.

19:38.010 --> 19:41.180
He didn't want to make a fuss
over a political issue.

19:41.930 --> 19:44.433
Then, do you still think
those trying to harm you

19:45.017 --> 19:47.477
are the ones who attacked
the spokesperson?

19:50.355 --> 19:51.607
[reporter 6] Wait. What's that?

19:52.149 --> 19:53.650
[bodyguard 3] Move out of the way.

19:53.734 --> 19:55.402
- What are you doing?
- [bodyguard 2] Move.

19:55.485 --> 19:56.945
[bodyguard 1] Stop. Don't go inside.

19:57.029 --> 19:58.739
- Hey.
- [bodyguard 3] You can't go inside.

19:58.822 --> 20:00.115
[people clamoring]

20:05.996 --> 20:09.458
PAIK JANG-HO'S GRANDSON,
PAIK UI-YONG'S SON

20:10.667 --> 20:13.545
I KNOW WHAT PAIK SA-EON DID

20:13.629 --> 20:15.005
[suspenseful music playing]

20:16.131 --> 20:17.382
[reporter 8] Share a few words!

20:31.939 --> 20:33.148
[music ends]

20:33.232 --> 20:36.026
[in English] Surprise!

20:36.109 --> 20:37.402
WE'RE IN THIS TOGETHER!

20:37.486 --> 20:39.279
[amusing music playing]

20:40.364 --> 20:41.531
THIS TOO SHALL PASS!

20:42.449 --> 20:43.283
[sighs wearily]

20:46.703 --> 20:50.082
[Young-woo] After thinking about
how to offer our support and comfort,

20:50.165 --> 20:51.792
we prepared this.

20:52.334 --> 20:53.585
Do you like it?

21:00.592 --> 21:01.426
Mr. Kang.

21:02.094 --> 21:02.928
Yes?

21:03.595 --> 21:05.055
[Sa-eon] Did you ask me

21:05.138 --> 21:07.307
to hurry to the office for this?

21:08.850 --> 21:11.937
When I took my first day off
in three years?

21:12.020 --> 21:13.230
Yes.

21:13.313 --> 21:14.940
You took your first day off in 3 years.

21:15.023 --> 21:16.858
We imagined how you felt,

21:16.942 --> 21:19.945
how difficult it must've been.

21:20.028 --> 21:22.114
[amusing music continues playing]

21:24.866 --> 21:25.701
[sighs]

21:25.784 --> 21:28.912
Since we prepared this anyway,
should we take a commemorative photo?

21:31.832 --> 21:32.833
[music ends]

21:32.916 --> 21:36.336
By the way, where's Mr. Park?

21:37.170 --> 21:38.880
[footsteps approaching]

21:38.964 --> 21:39.798
Sir!

21:45.220 --> 21:46.847
You've found his location?

21:46.930 --> 21:49.057
Yes, the reverse tracking is complete.

21:49.141 --> 21:51.351
[suspenseful music playing]

21:52.728 --> 21:54.021
[Sa-eon] Hajeong, Gyeonggi-do?

21:54.646 --> 21:56.398
[Do-jae] Does the location ring a bell?

21:59.276 --> 22:00.861
Are you going right now?

22:00.944 --> 22:03.113
- Then I'll come with--
- [Sa-eon] I'll go alone.

22:03.196 --> 22:04.865
Don't tell the police.

22:06.450 --> 22:07.284
Sir.

22:09.953 --> 22:11.079
Be careful.

22:12.164 --> 22:13.165
Great work.

22:18.670 --> 22:19.671
CHILDREN'S WELFARE CENTER

22:19.755 --> 22:22.049
- [director] Enjoy.
- [children] Okay!

22:22.132 --> 22:23.216
[indistinct chatter]

22:26.261 --> 22:28.930
[director] We're still eating
what you bought before.

22:29.014 --> 22:30.348
I appreciate it.

22:31.016 --> 22:31.850
That reminds me.

22:32.809 --> 22:36.354
Did you find out anything more
about what you asked me last time?

22:36.438 --> 22:37.856
That? No.

22:38.607 --> 22:41.818
I've been asking his peers
to try to find the twin brother…

22:41.902 --> 22:43.070
[inhales deeply]

22:43.153 --> 22:44.362
but no one knows anything.

22:46.448 --> 22:49.785
By the way, what about the newscaster
who came with you before?

22:50.285 --> 22:51.828
She didn't come today.

22:52.496 --> 22:53.330
Oh, her.

22:54.164 --> 22:55.624
She's probably working.

22:55.707 --> 22:57.375
She's not your girlfriend?

22:57.459 --> 23:00.212
Not at all. She's just a colleague.

23:01.338 --> 23:02.839
Then again… [chuckles softly]

23:03.298 --> 23:05.425
I remember your first love.

23:06.093 --> 23:08.095
She was nothing like her, right?

23:10.263 --> 23:11.389
My first love?

23:12.682 --> 23:13.850
Her name was…

23:15.102 --> 23:16.645
Hong Hee-joo, right?

23:18.647 --> 23:19.648
Oh.

23:20.524 --> 23:21.525
Yeah, well…

23:21.608 --> 23:23.110
[mellow music playing]

23:23.610 --> 23:26.404
You've got a great memory.

23:26.488 --> 23:27.739
Of course.

23:28.573 --> 23:31.660
She came to our center regularly
to volunteer for years.

23:31.743 --> 23:34.121
She even taught the kids to sign.

23:35.413 --> 23:37.499
I haven't seen her in so long.

23:38.458 --> 23:39.793
I wonder how she's doing.

23:42.420 --> 23:43.421
[door closes]

23:43.505 --> 23:45.799
[Yeon-hui] The chairman said
to bring you home for now,

23:45.882 --> 23:47.384
but no, you need to hold out.

23:47.467 --> 23:50.720
The moment you leave this house,
you can't come back.

23:50.804 --> 23:51.805
Also,

23:54.349 --> 23:56.226
I know who the culprit is.

23:56.768 --> 24:00.730
Who else would threaten Sa-eon
and talk about your marriage?

24:02.315 --> 24:04.025
Hong In-a. Who else?

24:05.443 --> 24:07.070
[scoffs] That brat…

24:07.654 --> 24:10.282
I could tell she was trying
to break you two apart.

24:10.365 --> 24:11.992
She must regret her choice now.

24:12.742 --> 24:14.286
What great timing, right?

24:14.911 --> 24:17.330
The election's soon,
things are going well,

24:17.414 --> 24:18.832
and she's trying to ruin it.

24:23.086 --> 24:23.920
Hey.

24:25.172 --> 24:26.756
Did you know she was back?

24:27.340 --> 24:29.467
What did she say?
Does she want everything back?

24:29.551 --> 24:30.927
You told her no, right?

24:32.304 --> 24:33.138
[Yeon-hui sighs]

24:33.680 --> 24:34.639
Don't see her again.

24:34.723 --> 24:36.850
Don't listen to anything she says, got it?

24:36.933 --> 24:38.018
[phone vibrates]

24:39.227 --> 24:41.104
[mysterious music playing]

24:42.814 --> 24:45.358
[kidnapper] Sis,
remember what I said before?

24:46.401 --> 24:49.487
You don't know anything about Paik Sa-eon.

24:50.447 --> 24:53.116
You can't even eat what's hand-fed to you.

24:53.200 --> 24:55.535
- [kidnapper] Don't you want to know?
- How could you only

24:55.619 --> 24:57.746
- take after your father?
- [kidnapper] Are you curious?

24:57.829 --> 25:00.665
Get it together,
or you'll end up like your father.

25:04.878 --> 25:06.338
Hey, I'm leaving.

25:11.593 --> 25:12.510
What is this?

25:13.261 --> 25:14.512
[car accelerating]

25:14.596 --> 25:15.722
[tires screeching]

25:19.726 --> 25:20.936
HBC JANG HYEOK-JIN

25:21.019 --> 25:21.978
[phone vibrating]

25:23.730 --> 25:25.523
- Hello?
- [Hyeok-jin] This was just posted.

25:26.066 --> 25:27.609
Take a look at what I sent.

25:28.360 --> 25:29.486
[phone vibrates]

25:35.617 --> 25:36.910
I KNOW WHAT PAIK SA-EON DID

25:37.702 --> 25:39.496
Do you think the culprit sent this?

25:39.579 --> 25:41.081
What's wrong with him?

25:41.164 --> 25:43.166
What grudge does he have against you?

25:43.250 --> 25:45.293
- [Sa-eon] I'm on my way to find out.
- What?

25:46.211 --> 25:47.045
Where?

25:47.128 --> 25:49.130
[mysterious music continues playing]

25:49.214 --> 25:50.298
[tires screeching]

25:50.966 --> 25:51.967
[car accelerating]

25:52.634 --> 25:53.468
Nothing!

26:00.225 --> 26:02.936
CALLS
PAIK SA-EON

26:10.193 --> 26:11.111
[phone vibrates]

26:13.738 --> 26:15.573
[Sang-woo] Hee-joo, how are you doing?

26:19.119 --> 26:21.454
[solemn music playing]

26:21.538 --> 26:22.706
[indistinct chatter]

26:27.127 --> 26:30.005
HEE-JOO, HOW ARE YOU DOING?

26:32.757 --> 26:35.427
ARE YOU OKAY?
I CAN'T REACH YOU, SO I'M WORRIED.

26:35.510 --> 26:37.095
[Hee-joo] It's been a while, Sang-woo.

26:38.054 --> 26:39.806
[Sang-woo] Hee-joo, have you been well?

26:43.018 --> 26:46.104
[Hee-joo] Sang-woo,
can you meet me right now?

26:46.187 --> 26:47.230
Right now?

26:51.109 --> 26:53.778
WILL PAIK SA-EON BLACKMAIL CASE
AFFECT PAIK UI-YONG'S ELECTION?

26:54.904 --> 26:56.197
[sighs]

26:57.574 --> 26:59.659
How are you going to handle this?

26:59.743 --> 27:02.203
There's a limit to what I can stop.

27:02.287 --> 27:05.040
The person to handle this
isn't me or the spokesperson.

27:05.790 --> 27:06.875
It's you.

27:07.917 --> 27:10.337
- Take responsibility and fix it.
- What?

27:11.421 --> 27:13.298
What kind of absurd nonsense is this?

27:15.175 --> 27:17.886
Didn't all of this happen
because of your daughters?

27:18.470 --> 27:21.473
If it'd gone as originally agreed,
this wouldn't be happening!

27:22.432 --> 27:24.851
Why give them the chance to find fault?

27:27.479 --> 27:28.730
It's all in the past,

27:29.689 --> 27:31.232
but since you brought it up,

27:31.941 --> 27:33.193
let me ask you something.

27:34.402 --> 27:36.112
Your family's Achilles' heel,

27:37.030 --> 27:40.241
are you sure it was taken care of
by Chairman Paik?

27:42.827 --> 27:44.496
[suspenseful music playing]

27:45.997 --> 27:47.040
No?

27:48.333 --> 27:49.667
Is there something left

27:50.335 --> 27:51.836
that hasn't been cleared away?

27:54.547 --> 27:55.548
Of course not.

27:55.632 --> 27:57.384
If, and I mean if,

27:58.468 --> 28:03.306
that thing shows up now
and holds you or me back,

28:04.766 --> 28:06.226
this time,

28:07.602 --> 28:09.270
I'll chop it

28:10.563 --> 28:12.273
into tiny pieces… [bangs table]

28:13.066 --> 28:15.068
from head to tail myself

28:16.403 --> 28:19.155
and neatly scatter them in your yard.

28:20.532 --> 28:23.618
So either look forward to it
or prepare yourself.

28:25.245 --> 28:27.455
I advise you to do something,
Candidate Paik.

28:32.460 --> 28:34.379
I advise you to repay me first.

28:38.383 --> 28:40.135
Shouldn't you at least pretend

28:41.302 --> 28:43.930
to repay the debt you owe me
from three years ago?

28:44.514 --> 28:46.182
[dramatic music playing]

28:49.310 --> 28:51.354
I'm talking about your eldest daughter.

28:55.608 --> 28:58.361
[Sang-woo] I'm glad nothing happened.

28:58.945 --> 29:01.740
So many incidents happened
after you started working there.

29:01.823 --> 29:04.492
I felt a little troubled.

29:05.785 --> 29:07.328
Thanks for your concern.

29:08.580 --> 29:09.831
But what's going on?

29:10.623 --> 29:11.666
What brings you here?

29:16.379 --> 29:20.049
The case you're investigating
on the program you're appearing on,

29:21.176 --> 29:24.012
didn't you say it was about a case
of missing orphans?

29:26.181 --> 29:27.891
Yeah, that's right.

29:28.892 --> 29:31.770
Can you tell me more about it?

29:33.062 --> 29:35.398
[intriguing music playing]

30:04.010 --> 30:05.053
[door opens]

30:06.262 --> 30:07.347
[door creaking]

30:09.724 --> 30:10.725
[door closes]

30:19.442 --> 30:21.361
[intriguing music continues playing]

30:56.980 --> 30:58.022
[music ends]

30:58.106 --> 30:59.566
[woman on TV] Help yourself!

31:00.608 --> 31:02.235
[man 1 on TV] Eat it before it cools.

31:04.195 --> 31:06.781
[woman on TV] You don't like it?
Those were good too.

31:08.116 --> 31:09.868
[man 1 on TV]
The meat was bursting out.

31:09.951 --> 31:11.494
It wasn't just like a sausage or ham.

31:11.578 --> 31:13.246
[woman on TV] Yeah. That's right.

31:13.329 --> 31:15.915
[man 2 on TV] What's it like?
What Korean food does it resemble?

31:15.999 --> 31:16.833
Nothing!

31:16.916 --> 31:17.917
[all laughing on TV]

31:18.710 --> 31:20.795
[man 2 on TV]
If this is how it's going to be,

31:20.879 --> 31:22.297
don't call it a seminar.

31:26.342 --> 31:27.719
[keys clacking]

31:29.345 --> 31:30.388
YOU DID IT

31:30.471 --> 31:32.390
YOU'RE THE KILLER

31:32.473 --> 31:33.766
[suspenseful music playing]

31:33.850 --> 31:36.269
PAIK SA-EON

31:44.986 --> 31:48.072
[man 1] The meat was bursting out.
It wasn't just like a sausage or ham.

31:48.156 --> 31:50.783
- [woman] Yeah. That's right.
- [man 2] What's it like?

31:50.867 --> 31:52.660
What Korean food does it resemble?

31:52.744 --> 31:53.578
[man 1] Nothing!

31:54.287 --> 31:56.456
MISSING ORPHAN CASE
CONTACT US IF YOU KNOW ANYTHING

31:56.539 --> 31:57.916
[suspenseful music playing]

32:07.967 --> 32:11.846
This house is where the orphanage kids
went in and never came out.

32:12.639 --> 32:14.474
Why is the door open?

32:16.017 --> 32:17.727
Does someone live here now?

32:17.810 --> 32:18.645
No.

32:19.187 --> 32:20.063
I don't think so.

32:21.439 --> 32:22.607
Did you go in?

32:22.690 --> 32:24.567
Yeah. Last time I came here.

32:27.195 --> 32:29.364
Hee-joo, why do you ask about the case?

32:30.490 --> 32:32.241
Do you know something about it?

32:38.873 --> 32:40.208
You're asking about it.

32:40.959 --> 32:42.877
And the spokesperson asked before.

32:44.128 --> 32:45.338
You're both very interested.

32:47.340 --> 32:49.092
We're coming back from covering a site.

32:49.842 --> 32:53.262
You know that we're doing a show together.

32:53.846 --> 32:56.808
- You-ri told me you asked her about me.
- [gasps]

32:58.601 --> 33:00.395
What's the story about?

33:03.314 --> 33:04.232
[crow caws]

33:05.817 --> 33:07.151
It's too late tonight.

33:07.235 --> 33:09.404
So let's come back during the day.

33:09.487 --> 33:11.781
[suspenseful music continues playing]

33:26.421 --> 33:27.588
[car accelerating]

33:35.930 --> 33:37.098
[phone vibrating]

33:39.934 --> 33:41.602
PAIK SA-EON

33:43.271 --> 33:45.231
Is there someone that calls you?

33:47.734 --> 33:48.735
[phone vibrating]

33:50.278 --> 33:51.112
Take it.

33:54.490 --> 33:55.658
You can take it.

33:58.578 --> 33:59.996
How could I?

34:00.913 --> 34:01.873
[Sang-woo scoffs]

34:02.707 --> 34:04.667
I guess there's someone who knows
besides me.

34:06.544 --> 34:07.670
Know what?

34:10.923 --> 34:12.675
That you can speak.

34:15.595 --> 34:16.763
[horn honking]

34:16.846 --> 34:18.181
[gripping music playing]

34:21.768 --> 34:22.602
What's that?

34:22.685 --> 34:23.686
[horn honking]

34:28.191 --> 34:29.525
[line ringing]

34:29.609 --> 34:30.651
HONG HEE-JOO

34:30.735 --> 34:31.611
[line disconnects]

34:31.694 --> 34:33.071
[horn honking]

34:33.154 --> 34:34.405
[tires screeching]

34:35.031 --> 34:36.157
[car accelerating]

34:36.741 --> 34:37.867
What are they doing?

34:37.950 --> 34:39.077
[horn honking]

34:44.874 --> 34:45.875
[car accelerating]

34:50.546 --> 34:52.131
- [tires screeching]
- [horn honking]

34:56.636 --> 34:58.221
[tires screeching]

35:01.682 --> 35:02.517
Is he crazy?

35:02.600 --> 35:03.559
[exhales nervously]

35:03.643 --> 35:04.644
[music ends]

35:10.149 --> 35:11.109
Don't get out.

35:14.320 --> 35:15.488
- Open it.
- Don't.

35:16.072 --> 35:18.241
We don't know why he's acting like this.

35:20.034 --> 35:20.868
Hee-joo.

35:22.912 --> 35:23.746
Hee-joo!

35:24.831 --> 35:26.082
What are you doing?

35:26.165 --> 35:27.250
Let go.

35:27.917 --> 35:29.919
[tense music playing]

35:37.760 --> 35:38.845
I'm warning you.

35:38.928 --> 35:41.472
Don't ever come near Hong Hee-joo again.

35:41.556 --> 35:42.640
Who are you to say that?

35:43.349 --> 35:45.977
What exactly is your relationship
with Hee-joo?

35:46.060 --> 35:47.186
You answer me first.

35:47.270 --> 35:50.523
How much do you know
about the Sinil Childcare Center incident?

35:51.399 --> 35:53.192
Have you found the culprit?

35:54.360 --> 35:55.194
Why do you ask--

35:55.278 --> 35:56.988
There'd be an investigation if they had!

35:59.740 --> 36:01.701
Do you already know who the culprit is?

36:02.618 --> 36:05.413
- So you're seeking revenge?
- [scoffs] "Revenge"?

36:07.081 --> 36:09.917
I don't know if I'm having
reasonable doubts about you

36:10.001 --> 36:11.878
or if it's just a misunderstanding,

36:12.920 --> 36:14.046
but stop here.

36:14.964 --> 36:15.965
Stop…

36:16.757 --> 36:17.884
digging into this case.

36:17.967 --> 36:20.803
Why do you care so much about it?

36:22.597 --> 36:24.182
What does it have to do with you?

36:25.308 --> 36:26.350
[music intensifies]

36:28.102 --> 36:31.189
What bothers me isn't the case, it's you.

36:32.148 --> 36:33.649
From the moment you appeared,

36:33.733 --> 36:36.319
the threats, kidnapping,
and explosions started.

36:37.945 --> 36:41.115
Is that really a coincidence?

36:41.699 --> 36:42.617
What?

36:50.041 --> 36:50.958
[engine starting]

36:52.752 --> 36:53.753
[car accelerating]

37:01.093 --> 37:01.969
[music fades]

37:11.020 --> 37:11.854
[Sa-eon sighs]

37:11.938 --> 37:13.481
Why did you come here?

37:18.486 --> 37:19.487
Because of this.

37:20.738 --> 37:21.656
It was sent to me.

37:21.739 --> 37:24.617
- [man 1] …a sausage or ham.
- [woman] Yeah. That's right.

37:24.700 --> 37:27.370
- [man 2] What food does it resemble?
- [man 1] Nothing!

37:29.705 --> 37:30.915
[tires screech]

37:43.302 --> 37:45.554
UNKNOWN CALLER
YOU DON'T KNOW ANYTHING ABOUT PAIK SA-EON.

37:56.148 --> 37:57.483
So did you go

37:59.026 --> 38:00.111
to ask Ji Sang-woo?

38:00.903 --> 38:02.989
I asked about the case.

38:03.072 --> 38:04.532
Why didn't you ask me?

38:05.700 --> 38:08.327
Were you scared to ask?

38:11.289 --> 38:12.623
Answer me, Hong Hee-joo.

38:15.876 --> 38:16.877
You're right.

38:17.628 --> 38:18.546
I was scared.

38:22.883 --> 38:23.718
[sighs]

38:24.218 --> 38:26.220
[somber music playing]

38:32.435 --> 38:33.352
[scoffs]

38:37.523 --> 38:38.357
Why?

38:39.692 --> 38:41.444
Are you scared and anxious

38:42.653 --> 38:43.904
that you might find…

38:46.324 --> 38:48.284
something shocking about me?

38:49.035 --> 38:50.202
Is that it?

38:56.292 --> 38:57.293
I've been scared,

38:58.836 --> 38:59.837
anxious,

39:01.756 --> 39:03.591
and wanted to run away many times.

39:05.843 --> 39:07.428
[slow music playing]

39:08.596 --> 39:10.848
I was afraid you'd find out
that I was 406,

39:12.516 --> 39:14.894
that you wouldn't forgive me,

39:17.521 --> 39:19.607
or that you'd never want to see me again.

39:21.233 --> 39:22.234
[sighs]

39:24.278 --> 39:26.030
I wanted to run away…

39:28.240 --> 39:31.077
before you found out about everything.

39:31.994 --> 39:34.163
So I am scared and anxious.

39:35.498 --> 39:36.957
That you might run away

39:37.541 --> 39:39.543
if I find out your secret,

39:42.088 --> 39:43.130
just like I wanted to.

39:45.174 --> 39:47.009
So I couldn't ask you.

39:49.178 --> 39:50.179
Because…

39:52.390 --> 39:54.183
I know what that's like.

39:58.979 --> 40:01.857
That's not the only thing I'm scared of.
Today, I…

40:05.361 --> 40:07.780
I've felt anxious ever since I woke up.

40:09.156 --> 40:11.158
[voice shaking] I was scared last night…

40:13.160 --> 40:14.495
was just a dream.

40:16.122 --> 40:17.123
The kind of dream

40:18.207 --> 40:20.418
that makes me break down in tears
when I wake up,

40:21.168 --> 40:23.421
feeling empty and sad.

40:23.504 --> 40:25.089
[sobbing]

40:31.137 --> 40:32.471
This kind of happiness

40:33.389 --> 40:35.099
would never happen to me.

40:35.182 --> 40:38.060
No one would love me this easily.

40:38.144 --> 40:41.480
That's never happened to me before,
so how could I?

40:51.824 --> 40:53.951
- How can I make you believe it?
- [Hee-joo crying]

40:54.785 --> 40:55.744
What can I do

40:57.746 --> 40:58.622
to ease your mind?

41:03.586 --> 41:04.670
[sighs deeply]

41:06.005 --> 41:07.548
Don't hide anything from me.

41:08.132 --> 41:09.383
Show me everything.

41:09.967 --> 41:12.011
I can handle anything.

41:14.346 --> 41:15.806
Don't be so sure of that.

41:15.890 --> 41:16.974
Why not?

41:19.560 --> 41:23.063
You knew I was 406,
yet you didn't abandon me.

41:23.147 --> 41:24.440
Let us

41:25.399 --> 41:27.318
show each other our worst

41:28.027 --> 41:29.320
and make it even.

41:30.779 --> 41:31.947
[dramatic song playing]

41:36.535 --> 41:37.786
Hong Hee-joo.

41:39.955 --> 41:41.248
If…

41:43.375 --> 41:45.211
something happens to me

41:47.463 --> 41:49.882
and the Paik Sa-eon you've known

41:50.466 --> 41:52.426
disappears from this world,

41:53.594 --> 41:57.723
even if I throw away the title
of Paik Jang-ho's grandson,

41:59.225 --> 42:01.602
Paik Ui-yong's son, and the spokesperson,

42:03.771 --> 42:05.022
just remember this.

42:07.858 --> 42:11.237
The only Paik Sa-eon
I want to leave behind in this world…

42:17.368 --> 42:19.161
is the one that belongs to Hong Hee-joo.

42:27.253 --> 42:28.254
[crying]

42:45.771 --> 42:46.605
[song ends]

42:47.898 --> 42:50.234
[Il-gyeong] In-a, why did you come back
without me knowing?

42:55.114 --> 42:57.032
When I said I couldn't marry him,

42:57.616 --> 42:59.243
I thought you'd force me to.

43:00.202 --> 43:02.246
But you let me go easily,

43:02.746 --> 43:04.248
so I was grateful

43:04.832 --> 43:06.083
yet a bit surprised.

43:06.917 --> 43:08.502
Was it all part of your plan?

43:10.254 --> 43:12.673
Were you the one who sent me those papers?

43:15.217 --> 43:16.594
[tense music playing]

43:18.345 --> 43:20.472
PAIK UI-YONG AND PAIK SA-EON
DNA NOT MATCHED

43:21.682 --> 43:22.516
[paper rustles]

43:26.395 --> 43:29.231
[In-a] When I think about it,
you didn't look so surprised.

43:29.815 --> 43:31.150
As if you already knew.

43:32.276 --> 43:33.110
No.

43:34.862 --> 43:37.948
There was no reason for you
to send it anonymously.

43:38.032 --> 43:40.242
You could've just told me.

43:40.326 --> 43:41.577
Stop talking nonsense.

43:42.161 --> 43:43.537
[In-a] What was the reason?

43:43.621 --> 43:45.831
Why did you make me
run away from that marriage?

43:47.041 --> 43:49.835
What's the contract you signed
with Chairman Paik?

43:50.586 --> 43:51.879
[Ui-yong] What did you just say?

43:51.962 --> 43:53.464
[gripping music playing]

43:53.547 --> 43:54.632
Your second daughter?

43:54.715 --> 43:55.549
Sir.

43:56.634 --> 43:59.887
Hundreds of wedding invitations
went out under In-a's name.

43:59.970 --> 44:04.224
Everyone knows that Paik Ui-yong's son
is engaged to Chungwoon family's eldest.

44:04.308 --> 44:07.561
Now you want to send your second daughter
down the aisle?

44:07.645 --> 44:09.396
[laughs dryly]

44:09.855 --> 44:11.565
[Ui-yong] This is a soap opera.

44:12.274 --> 44:15.402
Have you lost your mind
since your daughter ran off?

44:15.486 --> 44:17.821
Also, why should we take
your second daughter?

44:17.905 --> 44:20.866
Do you think
she's on the same level as Sa-eon?

44:20.949 --> 44:22.534
There's nothing more to discuss.

44:22.618 --> 44:25.079
- Let's prepare a statement.
- No one will know.

44:25.663 --> 44:28.248
Let's just fill the empty slot.

44:29.083 --> 44:31.418
You've done it before, so you know.

44:32.044 --> 44:33.587
It's easier than you think.

44:36.882 --> 44:38.592
[gripping music continues playing]

44:42.554 --> 44:43.931
Our two families…

44:46.600 --> 44:48.686
have a long-standing agreement.

44:55.401 --> 44:59.530
Chairman Paik kneeled before me
and made this promise.

45:01.657 --> 45:02.825
He promised to grant me

45:04.159 --> 45:05.285
anything I wanted,

45:05.369 --> 45:09.039
whenever and whatever it may be.

45:10.666 --> 45:12.292
IF THE CONFIDENTIALITY CLAUSE IS UPHELD,

45:12.376 --> 45:15.421
PARTY B MUST ACCOMMODATE ANY REQUEST
MADE BY PARTY A, WHENEVER, WHEREVER.

45:21.677 --> 45:23.470
PAIK JANG-HO
HONG IL-GYEONG

45:26.181 --> 45:27.474
[In-a] I heard it from her.

45:27.558 --> 45:29.893
Who is all ears and loose-tongued.

45:32.312 --> 45:34.356
But I'm sure you wouldn't just tell me,

45:35.232 --> 45:37.693
so I thought about it.

45:39.695 --> 45:41.196
The car accident when I was young.

45:42.030 --> 45:43.073
After that,

45:43.907 --> 45:45.409
you were mad for a while.

45:46.326 --> 45:50.664
You had the police and prosecutors
investigate and dig everything up.

45:51.498 --> 45:53.834
As if you'd make a culprit
if there wasn't one.

45:54.460 --> 45:55.294
But…

45:56.879 --> 45:58.547
why did you stop?

46:00.299 --> 46:01.425
No.

46:02.050 --> 46:04.178
Who made you stop?

46:04.261 --> 46:06.263
[tense music playing]

46:08.724 --> 46:10.225
[thunder rumbling]

46:17.149 --> 46:18.108
[inhales deeply]

46:18.192 --> 46:19.234
[exhales]

46:19.318 --> 46:21.403
Don't bring up the rotten past.

46:22.070 --> 46:24.948
Do you want to know
what you should be focusing on now?

46:27.534 --> 46:30.037
Did you hear
that Paik Sa-eon is being threatened?

46:30.621 --> 46:31.497
The culprit

46:32.456 --> 46:34.333
knows everything about Hee-joo.

46:35.375 --> 46:36.460
Hee-joo?

46:36.543 --> 46:37.544
That means…

46:38.962 --> 46:40.339
they know

46:41.381 --> 46:42.799
what happened to you,

46:43.550 --> 46:44.968
Sa-eon, and Hee-joo.

46:47.221 --> 46:50.224
[You-ri] How are you so sweet? [chuckles]

46:50.807 --> 46:55.354
What's your secret to maintaining
such a happy marriage?

46:55.437 --> 46:57.940
Well, there's nothing special.

46:58.023 --> 47:00.400
We just fill each other with what we lack

47:01.068 --> 47:03.529
and share what we have in excess.

47:03.612 --> 47:06.698
While doing that, we've become like one.

47:06.782 --> 47:08.283
I can't live without her now.

47:08.367 --> 47:09.910
[laughing]

47:09.993 --> 47:11.995
In such a harmonious home,

47:12.079 --> 47:16.166
I hear there have been some troubling
and worrying issues lately.

47:16.750 --> 47:20.170
It's about your son,
Spokesperson Paik Sa-eon.

47:20.254 --> 47:21.213
Yes, about that…

47:21.296 --> 47:23.465
"The threats and acts of terror

47:24.466 --> 47:26.051
were crimes of vengeance."

47:26.718 --> 47:28.971
"The victim provided the reason
for the threats."

47:29.555 --> 47:31.723
I hear there are various rumors.

47:32.516 --> 47:33.350
Yes.

47:33.850 --> 47:36.186
However, some insist
that that isn't the case

47:36.270 --> 47:39.565
and urge caution
against reckless speculation.

47:39.648 --> 47:43.652
I apologize for causing concern
to our supporters and the public

47:44.236 --> 47:46.655
who have trusted and watched over us.

47:47.364 --> 47:50.576
We promise to resolve this matter swiftly.

47:51.201 --> 47:52.369
However,

47:53.912 --> 47:54.913
to my son Sa-eon,

47:55.581 --> 47:59.585
who must be suffering more than anyone,

48:00.627 --> 48:01.628
as his mother,

48:02.921 --> 48:04.423
I want to say something.

48:05.132 --> 48:07.301
Goodness. That would be great.

48:07.384 --> 48:10.762
Now, look at the camera
and say what you have to say, please.

48:10.846 --> 48:11.930
Okay.

48:19.521 --> 48:20.397
[sniffles]

48:22.024 --> 48:24.026
[ominous music playing]

48:27.487 --> 48:28.614
Sa-eon.

48:29.865 --> 48:31.116
Do you remember?

48:32.659 --> 48:33.493
Remember…

48:36.038 --> 48:37.831
what I always said to you?

48:38.415 --> 48:40.292
- [banging on door]
- [boy crying]

48:43.879 --> 48:46.340
- [banging continues]
- [boy crying]

48:56.266 --> 48:58.143
[boy sobbing]

49:05.359 --> 49:06.693
[boy continues crying]

49:10.155 --> 49:10.989
I'm…

49:12.866 --> 49:14.284
not locking you up.

49:17.079 --> 49:18.580
I'm protecting you.

49:23.877 --> 49:24.878
I will…

49:27.089 --> 49:28.965
still protect you.

49:31.760 --> 49:32.969
I'll protect you,

49:34.930 --> 49:35.931
Sa-eon.

49:36.723 --> 49:37.641
[music ends]

49:37.724 --> 49:39.810
[Hee-joo] I'm sorry
for the worry I've caused.

49:39.893 --> 49:42.020
I'll work really hard.

49:42.979 --> 49:44.439
[Tae-kyeong] Don't be sorry.

49:44.523 --> 49:45.357
You did great.

49:46.525 --> 49:48.568
But I think you lost weight.

49:48.652 --> 49:49.528
[chuckles softly]

49:49.611 --> 49:51.488
How are you feeling?

49:52.322 --> 49:53.490
I'm okay.

49:54.741 --> 49:55.742
Now.

49:55.826 --> 49:57.411
To welcome you back to work,

49:57.494 --> 49:59.871
we've prepared a gift for you.

50:00.664 --> 50:01.873
A gift?

50:01.957 --> 50:04.209
You'll be the interpreter
for the spokesperson's speech

50:04.292 --> 50:06.878
at this year's
Environmental Climate Day event.

50:08.296 --> 50:09.381
[chuckles softly]

50:09.881 --> 50:11.842
See? I told you she'd be happy.

50:11.925 --> 50:12.759
You're right.

50:13.510 --> 50:16.471
I was worried it might be too much
since you just got back,

50:16.555 --> 50:18.014
but your face says otherwise.

50:18.098 --> 50:20.726
Let us know if it's too much for you.

50:20.809 --> 50:22.978
It's not at all!

50:23.061 --> 50:26.022
Just leave it to me,
and I'll do my best to prepare!

50:28.108 --> 50:31.027
Through this visit to France,
our government aims

50:31.111 --> 50:34.239
to strengthen the trust and friendship
between the two nations

50:34.322 --> 50:36.700
and establish a stepping stone

50:36.783 --> 50:38.702
into a cooperative partnership.

50:38.785 --> 50:42.205
Furthermore, we expect this visit
to contribute to the expansion

50:42.289 --> 50:44.791
and diversification
of our diplomatic outreach.

50:45.417 --> 50:46.251
That is all.

50:46.334 --> 50:48.295
[people murmuring]

50:52.007 --> 50:55.343
All right.
We will take questions from now on.

50:55.427 --> 50:56.970
- Spokesperson.
- Over here.

50:57.053 --> 50:58.430
[reporter 1] I have a question.

50:58.513 --> 51:00.807
- [reporter 2] Over here.
- There's so much enthusiasm.

51:00.891 --> 51:04.853
However, we'll only take questions
related to today's issues.

51:13.028 --> 51:14.279
How about a back briefing?

51:14.362 --> 51:17.324
- [reporter 3] A back briefing?
- I'll take questions on any topic.

51:17.991 --> 51:20.327
- Sir?
- [reporter 4] I have a question!

51:20.410 --> 51:22.996
- [reporter 5] Over here!
- Spokesperson, I have a question.

51:23.079 --> 51:24.581
- [reporter 6] Sir!
- [reporter 7] Here!

51:24.664 --> 51:25.499
Please.

51:25.582 --> 51:26.708
[suspenseful music playing]

51:26.792 --> 51:29.002
What did the blackmailer demand?

51:29.085 --> 51:31.797
And why didn't you report it
after the first threat?

51:32.464 --> 51:33.298
Well…

51:33.924 --> 51:34.925
Another question.

51:37.260 --> 51:39.554
"I know what you did, Paik Sa-eon."

51:39.638 --> 51:41.890
What do you think this means?

51:41.973 --> 51:42.974
Yes, any more?

51:46.144 --> 51:46.978
Go ahead.

51:48.021 --> 51:50.524
You firmly said
it was not political terrorism.

51:50.607 --> 51:52.025
How are you so sure?

51:54.945 --> 51:58.573
Surprisingly, it seems
you're all being careful around me.

51:59.908 --> 52:01.368
You can ask bolder questions.

52:02.077 --> 52:03.119
Let's be honest,

52:03.703 --> 52:05.914
you're all curious about one thing.

52:06.498 --> 52:09.042
You've all dug into me
and never found any dirt.

52:09.626 --> 52:12.712
So, what could be
Paik Sa-eon's deadly weakness?

52:13.964 --> 52:14.798
A woman?

52:14.881 --> 52:15.715
Gambling?

52:16.466 --> 52:17.300
Drugs?

52:17.384 --> 52:18.510
He's out of his mind.

52:18.593 --> 52:21.096
- Sir…
- I'm going to show you something,

52:21.179 --> 52:22.973
and I want you all to make use

52:23.056 --> 52:25.267
of your information
and investigative skills

52:25.350 --> 52:26.768
to solve this quiz.

52:27.352 --> 52:28.353
[music stops]

52:28.436 --> 52:31.231
The meat was bursting out.
It wasn't just like a sausage or ham.

52:31.314 --> 52:32.816
[woman on TV] Yeah. That's right.

52:33.441 --> 52:34.568
[man on TV] What's it like?

52:34.651 --> 52:36.444
- What Korean food does it resemble?
- Nothing!

52:36.528 --> 52:38.071
[laughter on TV]

52:40.240 --> 52:41.950
[suspenseful music continues]

52:42.033 --> 52:44.077
[Sa-eon] The video I just showed you

52:44.160 --> 52:46.997
is what I received from the blackmailer
just yesterday.

52:47.080 --> 52:50.041
But you can't tell what it's about,
can you?

52:50.125 --> 52:51.751
What does he want?

52:52.460 --> 52:54.421
What's he threatening me with?

52:55.088 --> 52:56.298
It's the same for me.

52:56.882 --> 52:59.718
So I need your help.

52:59.801 --> 53:00.886
So,

53:01.845 --> 53:02.929
what if we figure it out?

53:05.307 --> 53:09.227
The one who figures it out
will get an exclusive interview.

53:09.311 --> 53:10.770
[reporters exclaim, murmur]

53:22.240 --> 53:23.491
[Jin-e] Stop it.

53:24.075 --> 53:27.162
Why are you treating us
and even grilling the meat?

53:29.289 --> 53:30.790
It's all done. Please, eat.

53:31.374 --> 53:33.001
- Let's eat!
- Thank you.

53:35.378 --> 53:37.422
Mmm! It's so good.

53:38.089 --> 53:40.508
Right? Eat your fill.

53:40.592 --> 53:41.593
[sighs]

53:42.677 --> 53:44.137
Why aren't you eating?

53:44.220 --> 53:45.847
No, I am.

53:46.932 --> 53:47.974
What is it?

53:48.516 --> 53:49.351
Are you crying?

53:49.434 --> 53:51.353
I'm not crying.

53:51.436 --> 53:52.729
[Jin-e sniffling]

53:52.812 --> 53:54.481
The smoke got in my eye.

53:54.564 --> 53:57.025
There's no smoke here.

53:57.108 --> 53:58.109
[voice breaking] I mean…

53:59.569 --> 54:02.697
It feels like just yesterday
you were practicing sign language

54:02.781 --> 54:06.034
with those tiny, delicate hands,
fumbling this way and that.

54:06.117 --> 54:07.160
[crying]

54:07.243 --> 54:09.037
When did you grow up like this?

54:10.121 --> 54:12.791
Now you're the interpreter
for the presidential office

54:13.583 --> 54:15.251
and are treating us to galbi.

54:15.335 --> 54:16.419
[laughing]

54:17.212 --> 54:19.047
I'm so touched.

54:19.923 --> 54:21.383
I need to pull it together.

54:25.095 --> 54:26.137
What's this?

54:26.763 --> 54:27.639
Why is it so good?

54:27.722 --> 54:28.848
[interpreters] Mmm.

54:28.932 --> 54:31.059
You said your department
are regulars here.

54:31.142 --> 54:32.644
I can see why.

54:32.727 --> 54:35.814
I wanted to come here with you.

54:36.606 --> 54:37.649
Thanks.

54:37.732 --> 54:40.151
You're the only one who thinks of me.

54:42.195 --> 54:43.446
By the way, Hee-joo,

54:44.614 --> 54:46.783
you've gotten so much prettier.

54:46.866 --> 54:48.410
- [Hee-joo gulps]
- I thought the same.

54:48.493 --> 54:50.537
- Me too.
- [Jin-e] Right?

54:50.620 --> 54:55.291
You look more radiant.
There's definitely something different.

54:56.126 --> 54:57.127
Wait.

55:00.630 --> 55:01.840
Did you get work done?

55:01.923 --> 55:02.757
Laser? Fillers?

55:02.841 --> 55:03.925
[interpreter 1] Come on.

55:04.009 --> 55:05.093
No.

55:05.176 --> 55:06.553
I'm just kidding.

55:06.636 --> 55:07.887
[laughing]

55:08.304 --> 55:09.305
Hey.

55:09.389 --> 55:12.976
You got hired by the presidential office,

55:13.059 --> 55:16.229
and you get to work right next
to the respected spokesperson.

55:16.312 --> 55:17.897
Of course, you look good.

55:20.567 --> 55:21.443
But…

55:22.736 --> 55:27.365
the atmosphere at the presidential office
has been chaotic lately.

55:27.991 --> 55:29.743
Is the spokesperson okay?

55:30.326 --> 55:31.244
[interpreter 1] Right.

55:31.828 --> 55:34.706
Are the threats for real?

55:34.789 --> 55:37.042
There was the accident
at the company retreat too.

55:38.710 --> 55:40.628
How would Hee-joo know?

55:40.712 --> 55:41.796
Look here.

55:42.505 --> 55:43.798
Just eat some galbi.

55:43.882 --> 55:45.425
Ah. Mm.

55:45.508 --> 55:47.719
What is this? It's so good!

55:47.802 --> 55:49.637
[Jin-e] This is perilla pesto.

55:49.721 --> 55:51.389
A quiz?

55:52.098 --> 55:54.559
A quiz?

55:55.685 --> 55:59.355
I mean, why has our spokesperson
become so high-maintenance lately?

55:59.439 --> 56:02.567
Why does he keep causing trouble
without consulting us?

56:02.650 --> 56:04.819
- [phone ringing]
- See?

56:04.903 --> 56:07.155
There it is.
It must be an answer to the quiz!

56:08.823 --> 56:10.033
Spokesperson's office.

56:10.116 --> 56:11.367
Is this…

56:12.410 --> 56:15.330
the presidential spokesperson's office?

56:15.830 --> 56:17.749
[Young-woo] Yes, it is.
How can I help you?

56:17.832 --> 56:19.542
[suspenseful music playing]

56:19.626 --> 56:20.627
I have

56:21.920 --> 56:26.341
something I need to tell
Spokesperson Paik Sa-eon.

56:26.424 --> 56:29.928
FISHING SUPPLIES

56:30.011 --> 56:32.013
[suspenseful music continues playing]

56:46.402 --> 56:47.237
[music fades]

56:47.320 --> 56:48.530
[elevator dings]

57:08.842 --> 57:10.593
[elevator chimes]

57:10.677 --> 57:13.012
- [automated voice] Second floor.
- [elevator dings]

57:13.096 --> 57:14.055
Getting off.

57:16.850 --> 57:18.184
Hello.

57:20.311 --> 57:21.229
Hello.

57:26.234 --> 57:28.027
[mellow music playing]

57:42.542 --> 57:44.419
Did you have…

57:45.170 --> 57:46.588
lunch?

57:49.841 --> 57:50.675
Interpreter.

57:51.551 --> 57:52.385
Hong.

57:54.262 --> 57:55.096
Hee.

57:55.722 --> 57:57.390
Joo.

57:58.099 --> 58:00.477
I did. What about you?

58:02.520 --> 58:03.438
So did I.

58:04.898 --> 58:06.649
Your sign language has improved.

58:08.735 --> 58:11.654
I've been practicing hard.

58:12.655 --> 58:13.656
Am I…

58:13.740 --> 58:14.908
good?

58:15.658 --> 58:17.952
Yes. It's rewarding to have taught you.

58:28.546 --> 58:29.506
I'll see you later.

58:30.298 --> 58:33.176
Okay, see you at home.

58:36.262 --> 58:38.932
I won't be late.

58:47.857 --> 58:48.858
[elevator dings]

58:55.198 --> 58:57.200
[mellow music continues playing]

59:28.648 --> 59:29.732
Sir?

59:29.816 --> 59:31.484
A call came in a moment ago.

59:31.568 --> 59:32.402
This…

59:36.322 --> 59:37.156
Come in.

59:55.717 --> 59:57.218
I have something to pass along.

59:59.262 --> 01:00:00.430
HE'S ALIVE

01:00:01.806 --> 01:00:03.016
Is this all?

01:00:03.099 --> 01:00:05.018
He hung up after saying this.

01:00:05.101 --> 01:00:08.521
So I immediately looked up
the caller's number,

01:00:09.147 --> 01:00:10.440
and a business came up.

01:00:11.024 --> 01:00:12.567
[ominous music playing]

01:00:12.650 --> 01:00:13.943
A business?

01:00:14.027 --> 01:00:16.821
JUAN FISHING

01:00:20.325 --> 01:00:22.577
[ominous music intensifies]

01:00:36.257 --> 01:00:37.258
[phone vibrates]

01:00:38.676 --> 01:00:41.346
Hey. Pictures from the retreat
have been posted.

01:00:41.429 --> 01:00:43.431
[Tae-kyeong] Really? I want to see.

01:00:49.771 --> 01:00:50.980
Did they turn out well?

01:00:51.481 --> 01:00:52.523
- Let's see.
- [Won-bin] Wow.

01:00:52.607 --> 01:00:54.359
Everyone looks great. [laughs]

01:00:54.942 --> 01:00:56.778
[Tae-kyeong] Mr. Jeong,
you came out great.

01:01:20.259 --> 01:01:22.261
[emotional music playing]

01:01:39.946 --> 01:01:41.948
[emotional music continues playing]

01:01:43.241 --> 01:01:44.450
Wait for me.

01:02:08.808 --> 01:02:10.810
[emotional music rises]

01:02:41.257 --> 01:02:42.800
[music fades]

01:02:42.884 --> 01:02:44.886
[eerie music playing]

01:02:49.390 --> 01:02:51.768
[man] He's alive.

01:02:53.311 --> 01:02:54.395
[Sa-eon] He's alive?

01:02:55.938 --> 01:02:58.441
Could it be him?

01:02:58.524 --> 01:03:00.151
[eerie music continues playing]

01:03:02.612 --> 01:03:03.863
[water splashes]

01:03:05.406 --> 01:03:07.241
[boy gasping]

01:03:09.869 --> 01:03:10.953
[boy] Help!

01:03:11.037 --> 01:03:12.747
[splashing]

01:03:18.586 --> 01:03:19.879
[boy gasping] Please help!

01:03:19.962 --> 01:03:21.047
Help…

01:03:22.632 --> 01:03:24.050
[eerie music intensifies]

01:03:27.345 --> 01:03:28.387
[boy gasping]

01:03:30.556 --> 01:03:31.933
[boy gasping]

01:03:36.062 --> 01:03:37.897
[gasping]

01:03:37.980 --> 01:03:39.732
[tense music playing]

01:03:40.441 --> 01:03:41.442
[young Sa-eon gasping]

01:03:41.526 --> 01:03:42.777
I told you not to come out.

01:03:43.569 --> 01:03:44.737
Go inside.

01:03:53.538 --> 01:03:55.957
[tense music continues playing]

01:04:03.965 --> 01:04:05.091
PAIK SA-EON

01:04:05.174 --> 01:04:06.259
[Hee-joo] Will you be late?

01:04:14.308 --> 01:04:15.935
[doorbell chimes]

01:04:16.018 --> 01:04:16.936
[music fades]

01:04:45.339 --> 01:04:48.050
This feels so strange.

01:04:48.759 --> 01:04:52.305
This house was supposed to be
my newlywed house.

01:04:56.350 --> 01:04:58.436
[Hee-joo] I have something to ask you.

01:04:58.978 --> 01:04:59.812
Go ahead.

01:05:03.107 --> 01:05:04.400
[Hee-joo] Why did you come back?

01:05:07.945 --> 01:05:10.364
If you're trying to reclaim what's yours…

01:05:10.448 --> 01:05:12.033
Shouldn't you ask first

01:05:12.617 --> 01:05:14.785
why I left in the first place?

01:05:15.536 --> 01:05:17.455
[suspenseful music playing]

01:05:26.881 --> 01:05:28.466
JUAN FISHING

01:05:33.763 --> 01:05:34.722
Father told me

01:05:35.306 --> 01:05:37.975
that Sa-eon's blackmailer knows everything

01:05:38.726 --> 01:05:40.770
about you and this marriage.

01:05:41.604 --> 01:05:43.147
Then you should also know

01:05:43.856 --> 01:05:45.775
why I refused this marriage.

01:05:46.484 --> 01:05:47.652
The reason…

01:05:49.195 --> 01:05:51.197
you had to marry him in my place.

01:06:02.166 --> 01:06:03.000
[gasps]

01:06:03.084 --> 01:06:05.169
[coughing]

01:06:15.805 --> 01:06:17.014
Wake up!

01:06:17.098 --> 01:06:18.474
Wake up!

01:06:20.267 --> 01:06:24.105
[In-a] There's more to Paik Sa-eon
than you think.

01:06:26.482 --> 01:06:27.483
[grunting]

01:06:32.029 --> 01:06:33.072
[grunting]

01:06:34.782 --> 01:06:35.992
[groans]

01:06:38.327 --> 01:06:40.538
[soft emotional music playing]

01:06:51.382 --> 01:06:52.967
Did you know already?

01:06:55.511 --> 01:06:56.595
It doesn't matter?

01:06:57.972 --> 01:06:59.932
[emotional music intensifies]

01:07:00.016 --> 01:07:00.933
[Sa-eon] Hong Hee-joo.

01:07:01.809 --> 01:07:03.019
If…

01:07:04.061 --> 01:07:05.813
something happens to me

01:07:08.107 --> 01:07:10.526
and the Paik Sa-eon you've known

01:07:11.110 --> 01:07:13.070
disappears from this world,

01:07:14.196 --> 01:07:18.367
even if I throw away the title
of Paik Jang-ho's grandson,

01:07:19.869 --> 01:07:22.246
Paik Ui-yong's son, and the spokesperson,

01:07:23.247 --> 01:07:24.540
just remember this.

01:07:25.249 --> 01:07:27.752
[explosion]

01:07:35.593 --> 01:07:39.180
The only Paik Sa-eon
I want to leave behind in this world…

01:07:42.141 --> 01:07:44.351
is the one that belongs to Hong Hee-joo.

01:07:44.435 --> 01:07:45.269
[music fades]

01:07:45.352 --> 01:07:48.272
WHEN THE PHONE RINGS

01:07:49.315 --> 01:07:50.399
Did they turn out well?

01:07:50.483 --> 01:07:52.068
[Tae-kyeong] Yes.

01:08:17.384 --> 01:08:19.053
[romantic song playing]

01:09:31.292 --> 01:09:34.211
WHEN THE PHONE RINGS

01:09:34.295 --> 01:09:35.629
[Hee-joo] What is this?

01:09:35.713 --> 01:09:38.007
What in the world happened?

01:09:38.591 --> 01:09:41.010
[Sang-woo] There's one thing I'm sure of.

01:09:41.093 --> 01:09:43.304
He wasn't hiding you

01:09:43.387 --> 01:09:44.763
but protecting you.

01:09:44.847 --> 01:09:47.600
[In-a] I've been curious about this.

01:09:47.683 --> 01:09:50.186
Who does Spokesperson Paik take after?

01:09:50.269 --> 01:09:52.855
[Hee-joo] I wonder what his real name is.

01:09:52.938 --> 01:09:56.192
[Sa-eon] Even if I'm not
the Paik Sa-eon you knew,

01:09:56.275 --> 01:09:57.610
does it not matter?

01:09:57.693 --> 01:09:59.195
[Hee-joo] It didn't matter to you.

01:10:00.863 --> 01:10:02.281
It's my turn now.

01:10:03.449 --> 01:10:05.492
It's my turn to protect you.

01:10:09.747 --> 01:10:11.749
Subtitle translation by: Sue Mounce
